request: Make the output easier to read. --behaviour

governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" could mean several different output changes, and each would need its own testable contract. Right now `todo list` prints only "[ ] title" lines. It doesn't show ids, which `complete` needs, and it doesn't show due dates, even though they're saved. I need to know which change you want before I commit owners to a format.)
governor asks: Which of these do you mean by "easier to read"? You can pick more than one.
(a) Show each todo's id in `todo list`, e.g. "#1 [ ] buy milk", so you know what to pass to `todo complete`.
(b) Show due dates when a todo has one, e.g. "#1 [ ] buy milk (due 2026-11-01)".
(c) Line up the columns (id, checkbox, title, due date) so they form a table.
(d) Sort the list, e.g. open todos first, then by due date.
(e) Add a summary line, e.g. "2 open, 1 done".
(f) Add terminal colour, e.g. dim the done todos.
(g) Change other messages too ("Added #1", "Completed #2", the error text).
If you have an exact list layout in mind, please paste a sample of the output you want for the three fixture todos.

